Subject: A builtin namespace object settles all its lazy members at the first touch

What this does
  - The first materialisation of a JS_AUTOINIT_ID_PROP property on a plain, non-exotic JS_CLASS_OBJECT builtin (Math, JSON, Reflect, Atomics, Intl-style namespaces; not the global object, not Object.prototype) materialises every lazy function member of that object in shape order (JS_AutoInitProperty -> js_autoinit_one per member). Test knob (QJS_KIT_TEST_KNOBS builds only): env QJS_NO_BUILTIN_SETTLE switches it off.

Why we need it
  Each js_autoinit_one calls js_shape_prepare_update, which clones the shape while a cache holds it (or moves it in place). Math's shape changed three times in raytrace's first rayTrace call (pow, max, hypot read at three sites), so the old backend's per-site PIC cells went stale and the function was gated off for good.

Soundness
  Property order, attributes and values are those of the eager definition (the same entries instantiated by the same function, in definition order); only the time moves earlier. The instantiation functions create C functions and read nothing of the object.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -13783,16 +13783,17 @@
